# Accepted vulnerability advisories for `pnpm run audit:supply-chain` and the
# matching CI scan in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# Both scans read this file, so an entry here suppresses the finding locally and
# in CI alike. Add one only with a maintainer's reason for why the advisory is
# unreachable and a time-bounded follow-up, per docs/supply-chain-security.md.
# One advisory ID per line, e.g.:
#
#   CVE-0000-00000  # unreachable: <reason>; revisit by <date>

# braces 3.0.3 has no patched release for deeply nested glob patterns.
# It is used only by development tooling (Jest, webpack/Docusaurus, file
# watchers and semantic-release). Glob patterns come from repository/tool
# configuration; filenames, request paths and commit text are match subjects,
# not patterns. The WebSocket integration proxy does not configure a glob
# path filter. No shipped Web3 runtime dependency exposes braces to RPC input.
# Upstream: https://github.com/micromatch/braces/issues/70
# Remove this exception when a fix ships or the pattern input boundary changes.
CVE-2026-93687  # unreachable: tooling-only, trusted glob patterns; revisit by 2026-11-04
